{"tool_name":"chagasdb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"chagasdb","home":"https://chagasdb.tagc.univ-amu.fr","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Manual-curated database regrouping published results referenced in Pubmed.","addition_date":"2024-01-02T01:41:01.150111Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:25:34.821693Z","tool_type":["Database portal"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:chagasdb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"christophe.chevillard@univ-amu.fr","name":"Christophe Chevillard","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5269-8813","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"edecunha@gmail.com","name":"Edecio Cunha-Neto","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3699-3345","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"lionel.spinelli@univ-amu.fr","name":"Lionel Spinelli","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9228-8141","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Data retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2422"},{"term":"Database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2421"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"}]}],"name":"ChagasDB","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/database/baad037","metadata":{"abstract":"Chagas disease is a parasitical disease caused by Trypanosoma cruzi which affects \u223c7 million people worldwide. Per year, \u223c10 000 people die from this pathology. Indeed, \u223c30% of humans develop severe chronic forms, including cardiac, digestive or neurological disorders, for which there is still no treatment. In order to facilitate research on Chagas disease, a manual curation of all papers corresponding to 'Chagas disease' referenced on PubMed has been performed. All deregulated molecules in hosts (all mammals, humans, mice or others) following T. cruzi infection were retrieved and included in a database, named C